diff --git a/docs/en/experimental-idle-compaction.md b/docs/en/experimental-idle-compaction.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/en/experimental-idle-compaction.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Experimental process-local idle compaction (V3 candidate)
+
+This is a test candidate, not a production reclamation guarantee. It retains
+native busy-admission retries and adds an opt-in mechanism for overwritten
+chunks that never reach ordinary Write thresholds, including low-count tails
+left after a compaction snapshot.
+
+Enable with `juicefs mount --idle-compact-delay=2m ...` (default `0`, disabled).
+`--no-bgjob` and read-only mounts disable the new worker. Positive configured
+delays below one second are clamped to one second by metadata config validation.
+
+Only successful writes performed by this metadata client create tracking entries;
+there is no volume scan, metadata format change, or restart discovery. Each entry
+uses a write generation so writes arriving during an older batch are retained.
+The worker waits until metadata Read/Write has been quiet, checks overlap using
+latest-wins slice reconstruction, and reuses ordinary compaction and engine CAS
+replacement/deletion. Valid non-overlapping slices are not rewritten.
+
+The new worker is serial and starts at most one batch per timer tick (at most
+once a second for a delay of two minutes). It does not start a batch while an
+existing compactor is active or while metadata IO has resumed during inspection.
+An already started object RPC is not preempted when foreground IO resumes: up to
+one idle batch may overlap it. This is NOT a bandwidth limiter, global cluster
+idle detector, or a guarantee of zero foreground performance impact. Multiple
+clients each have their own worker. The native ordinary admission gate is unchanged.
+
+Tracking is process-local and capped at 65,536 distinct chunks per client.
+Overflow increments `juicefs_idle_compact_queue_overflow_total` and emits a
+rate-limited warning: chunks that overflow are not guaranteed to be reclaimed.
+The inherited native busy retry map is separate and remains uncapped.
+Pending/check/attempt metrics are also exported. Errors or no progress retain
+tracked entries with cooldown/exponential backoff, capped at five minutes;
+the worker cannot guarantee reclamation while backend errors persist.
+
+Session cancellation stops new idle work and discards the process-local tracking.
+An in-flight object compaction must finish before the new worker joins; there is
+no unsafe forced cancellation. After restart/remount, pre-existing untracked
+history requires new writes or controlled maintenance. Other clients' writes
+are not discovered. Shared slice references and trash retention are still
+respected by the original metadata engine.
+
+Accept changes using no-user-read idle observations before final CRC. Reading
+files can independently trigger ordinary compaction and must not be used to
+manufacture a reclamation pass. Real TiKV/Ceph and long-duration validation are
+still required before deployment.
